# Rebuild and update after every task

When you finish any task that changes code, config or anything else the running app uses, rebuild and update the local install before you report back. Run commands from the repo root.

Rebuild and update the local install (`%LOCALAPPDATA%\Janus\Janus.exe`). The script builds a new Janus.exe, closes the running app, replaces the exe and restarts the service, keeping `settings.json` and logs:
```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\install-local.ps1
```
Use `.\scripts\reinstall.ps1` only if the user asks for a full reinstall.

**Never wipe data.** Don't remove volumes, databases, settings or logs (no `docker compose down -v`, no remove/uninstall scripts) unless the user explicitly asks.

**If the update fails,** fix it if your change caused it and run it again. Don't report the task as done while the app is broken. If the failure isn't related to your change, report it clearly.

**Verify.** Run `janus status` (or `janus doctor`) in a new terminal and confirm it is running the new build. Mention the result in your final reply.

Skip these steps only for tasks that don't affect the running app, such as answering questions or editing docs.